{"abstract":"Purpose In this paper, we introduce the CRISPS (CRoss-domaIn relevance aSPects Scheme) coding scheme for complex information needs in the four leisure domains of books, games, movies and music. It categorizes the relevance aspects people consider when searching for these resources. The coding scheme and findings help search engines to better support complex information needs, both by prioritizing which aspects are easier to classify automatically and by determining which information sources should be considered. Design/methodology/approach A cross-domain classification scheme for relevance aspects and information needs in casual leisure domains (CRISPS) is developed and applied. The paper provides the documentation of the scheme development and annotation process as well as a detailed, large-scale analysis of 2000 requests (500 per domain) and relevance aspects for four domains as expressed in complex search requests in everyday life information seeking posted to online forums. Findings We identify and discuss relevance aspect frequencies, information need types and the described search process of the requests. Furthermore, the coding scheme development and the annotation process are documented and reflected on. Originality/value This is the first categorization and analysis of complex information needs in these four leisure domains combined. The coding scheme and findings can be used to develop new types of search interfaces that incorporate the kinds of relevance aspects identified in the scheme, allowing to express complex needs in the form of structured queries.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Skov, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-785915"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Casual leisure search","Classification","Complex search tasks","Cross domain","Information need","Relevance aspects"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding complex casual leisure information needs an analysis of search requests for books games movies and music","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://doi.org/10.1108/JD-03-2024-0070","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-785915","identifier":[{"id":"85208116607","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6066ed0e-4921-4813-aec6-9da9789174a6"],"keyword":["Casual leisure search","Classification","Complex search tasks","Cross domain","Information need","Relevance aspects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F5FA77A7A7A16BFC32AA66B138A5FF5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/jd-03-2024-0070","issn":["00220418","17587379"],"issn_org":["00220418"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Documentation","pages":"168-194","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing Limited","status":"p","title":"Journal of Documentation","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208116607"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6066ed0e-4921-4813-aec6-9da9789174a6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Understanding complex casual leisure information needs : an analysis of search requests for books, games, movies and music","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-785915","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The rapidly increasing popularity of LLM-powered chatbots has led to them being used for a increasing number of different tasks by the general public. One of these tasks is searching for information instead of using a search engine. Previous work has shown that complex search tasks can be problematic for traditional search engines to solve, but little is known about the capability of LLMs on the same task. We compared four LLMs on their capability to answer a specific type of complex search task: known-item requests from casual leisure domains. We constructed a test collection by gathering known-item requests for books, games and movies from online forums along with verified answers by the original requester. We prompted four LLMs multiple times with the same prompt and analyzed the results with respect to accuracy and the degree to which answers were fabricated by the LLM. Our results show that LLMs are not particularly effective in fulfilling these complex casual leisure needs, but there are are big differences between LLMs and across domains.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Hall, Mark","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Skov, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-786480"],"event":{"end":"2025-03-28","place":"Melbourne, au","start":"2025-03-24","title":"CHIIR '25: 2025 ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","The Open University"],"keyword":["Hallucinations","Information needs","LLMs","Retrieval","known item needs"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the zero shot known item retrieval capabilities of llms for casual leisure information needs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3698204.3716466","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work of Toine Bogers was supported by the Pioneer Centre for AI, DNRF grant number P1. The authors acknowledge the Woi wurrung and Boon wurrung language groups of the eastern Kulin Nation on whose unceded lands ACM SIGIR CHIIR 2025 was hosted. We pay our respect to their Elders past and present and extend that respect to all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples today and their connections to land, sea, sky, and community."],"id":"S01-000.00-786480","identifier":[{"id":"105005288104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f2cfe311-f874-4f26-9d13-778a51a361ae"],"keyword":["Hallucinations","LLMs","casual leisure","information needs","known-item needs","retrieval","tip-of-the-tongue"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3CF240B505F69F7EB0DE052291B24074"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/781250275/3698204.3716466.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3698204.3716466","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"the open university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Open University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Challenges and movements in performing digitalization","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","name":"Bogers, Toine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"hallpau","last":"Hall","name":"Hall, Mark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"George","key":"buchananpedh","last":"Buchanan","name":"Buchanan, George","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Haiming","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Haiming","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dana","key":"mckaypedh","last":"McKay","name":"McKay, Dana","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Douglas","key":"oardpedh","last":"Oard","name":"Oard, Douglas","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3698204.3716466","eisbn":["9798400712906"],"pages":"316-325","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"CHIIR 2025 - Proceedings of the 2025 ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005288104"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f2cfe311-f874-4f26-9d13-778a51a361ae"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring the Zero-Shot Known-Item Retrieval Capabilities of LLMs for Casual Leisure Information Needs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-786480","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This poster abstract reports from a literature review on managerial use of AI for people leadership purposes identifying a research gap in our understanding of the lived practice of AI-usage for personnel related aspects of the leadership role in theory and practice. Although AI-assisted leadership is still in its infancy, larger corporations already adopt algorithmic leadership practices, emphasizing the need to explore and capture these developments in the expectation of widespread adoption in the (near) future. We report from the identification and analysis of a corpus of 66 research articles, identifying core themes including trust, flexibility, and correspondence with existing work tasks, pointing out limitations as well as highlighting implications for future research. We wish to ignite an all-inclusive debate on the exploration of AI-augmented leadership using our poster as a springboard for knowledge sharing and network building. We believe that the topic is interesting to both CTO-members and academy members generally. To lead traffic to our poster, small flyers will be handed out at the conference, and a short digital visitor survey will be administered to capture insights (accessible through QR code when poster is not staffed) and invite to post-poster networking.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rikke Kristine","Svarre, Tanja","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805354"],"event":{"end":"2025-07-29","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2025-07-25","title":"Academy of Management Annual Meeting","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Rikke Kristine"],"keyword":["AI","AI literacy","Algorithmic management","Articificial Intelligence","Digital dannelse","Human resource management","Kunstig intelligens","Ledelse","Literature review","Personaleledelse","Responsible AI","algoritmisk ledelse"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leadership in the age of ai exploring managerial ai enabled people leadership in practice","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-805354","ids":["aau-a7ca8927-8348-4663-ab63-69d442ee05a3"],"keyword":["AI","AI literacy","AI-assisted leadership","AI-assisted people managment","AI-driven leadership","AI-enabled leadership","AI-enabled people management","AI-ledelse","AI-supported leadership","AI-supported people leadership","AI-understøttet ledelse","Algorithmic management","Articificial Intelligence","Digital dannelse","Human Resource Management","Kunstig intelligens","Ledelse","Literature Review","Organizational AI capability","Personaleledelse","Responsible AI","algoritmisk ledelse"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9FF5367FB5829D424C3B2E0800216776"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Organization, Work & Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Organization, Work and Management","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rikke Kristine","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6622b183-562b-4061-87c3-69813fc17c94","name":"Nielsen, Rikke Kristine","orcid":"0000-0001-5828-5617","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tanja","key":"svarrepau","last":"Svarre","locid":"b3a9c3be-381a-4ac8-89d6-f5f118e9705b","name":"Svarre, Tanja","orcid":"0000-0002-5468-0406","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","name":"Bogers, Toine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a7ca8927-8348-4663-ab63-69d442ee05a3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Leadership in the Age of AI – Exploring Managerial AI-Enabled People Leadership in Practice","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805354","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"While there have been several studies on how users experience algorithmic recommendations and their explanations, we know relatively little about human recommendations and which item aspects humans highlight when describing their own recommendation needs. A better understanding of human recommendation behavior could help us design better recommender systems that are more attuned to their users. In this paper, we take a step towards such understanding by analyzing a Reddit community dedicated to requesting and providing for recommendations: /r/ifyoulikeblank. After a general analysis of the community, we provide a more detailed analysis of the prevalent music requests and the example items used to ask for these recommendations. Finally, we compare these human recommendations to algorithmic recommendations to better characterize their differences. We conclude by discussing the implications of our work for recommender systems design.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cao, Thi Binh Minh","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798555"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","title":"iConference"},"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human Recommendation","Mixed methods","Music Recommendation","Narrative driven Recommendation","Reddit"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"if i like blank what else will i like analyzing a human recommendation community on reddit","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85192194248","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798555","identifier":[{"id":"85192194248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b7c54fb5-3b09-4d72-8428-ae6b61649d22"],"keyword":["Human Recommendation","Mixed Methods","Music Recommendation","Narrative-driven Recommendation","Reddit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-8F6AC8BB5F77153B3BDB07D74C37F470"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thi Binh Minh","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Thi Binh Minh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"e726f512-d3fd-4d89-962a-3aa9f532a52f","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-57850-2_6","pages":"70-83","series":"LNCS","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 iConference","volume":"14596"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192194248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b7c54fb5-3b09-4d72-8428-ae6b61649d22"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“If I Like BLANK, What Else Will I Like?”: Analyzing a Human Recommendation Community on Reddit","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798555","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"While there have been several studies on how users experience algorithmic recommendations and their explanations, we know relatively little about human recommendations and which item aspects humans highlight when describing their own recommendation needs. A better understanding of human recommendation behavior could help us design better recommender systems that are more attuned to their users. In this paper, we take a step towards such understanding by analyzing a Reddit community dedicated to requesting and providing for recommendations: /r/ifyoulikeblank. After a general analysis of the community, we provide a more detailed analysis of the prevalent music requests and the example items used to ask for these recommendations. Finally, we compare these human recommendations to algorithmic recommendations to better characterize their differences. We conclude by discussing the implications of our work for recommender systems design.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cao, Thi Binh Minh","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-757377"],"event":{"end":"2024-04-26","place":"Changchun, cn","start":"2024-04-15","title":"19th International Conference on Wisdom, Well-Being, Win-Win, iConference 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bogers, Toine"],"keyword":["Human Recommendation","Mixed methods","Music Recommendation","Narrative driven Recommendation","Reddit"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"if i like blank what else will i like analyzing a human recommendation community on reddit","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85192194248&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-757377","identifier":[{"id":"85192194248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-de76135e-f0ec-4a35-a78c-665b0883b4a7"],"keyword":["Human Recommendation","Mixed Methods","Music Recommendation","Narrative-driven Recommendation","Reddit"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-8F6AC8BB5F77153B3BDB07D74C37F470"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thi Binh Minh","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","locid":"69205824-580e-4844-aa97-338ef55d809d","name":"Cao, Thi Binh Minh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Isaac","key":"sserwangapedh","last":"Sserwanga","name":"Sserwanga, Isaac","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Hideo","key":"johopedh","last":"Joho","name":"Joho, Hideo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jie","key":"mapedh","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Jie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Preben","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Preben","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan","key":"wupedh","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Dan","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Masanori","key":"koizumipedh","last":"Koizumi","name":"Koizumi, Masanori","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne J.","key":"gillilandpedh","last":"Gilliland","name":"Gilliland, Anne J.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-57850-2_6","eisbn":["9783031578502"],"isbn":["9783031578496"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"70-83","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"19th International Conference, iConference 2024, Changchun, China, April 15–26, 2024, Proceedings, Part I","title":"Wisdom, Well-Being, Win-Win"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192194248"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-de76135e-f0ec-4a35-a78c-665b0883b4a7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"“If I Like BLANK, What Else Will I Like?” : Analyzing a Human Recommendation Community on Reddit","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-757377","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Across all scientific fields, there is an increased focus on the impact of scientific research: what academic and societal benefits does it provide? This question has spurred the development of a variety of different approaches to impact assessment, each appropriate in different circumstances. In this paper, we study the academic impact of the CHIIR community through a comprehensive analysis of the work published in the 2016-2023 CHIIR conference series. We collect citation counts, citing documents, and altmetrics scores for all CHIIR publications to determine their academic impact across a variety of different attributes of the CHIIR publications. In addition, we analyze a subset of citation contexts in the papers that have cited CHIIR publications to analyze how they are being used and what that means for their potential impact. Finally, we attempt to predict which properties of CHIIR publications are most predictive of future impact.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gaede, Maria","Bogers, Toine","Hall, Mark Michael","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Larsen, Birger"],"cuid":["S02-094.72-792753"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2024-03-14","place":"Sheffield, gb","start":"2024-03-10","title":"2024 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Open University Milton Keynes","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","The Open University"],"keyword":["Citation analysis","IMPACT","Interactive information retrieval","Re use","Sharing"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact of chiir publications a study of eight years of chiir","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3627508.3638338","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.72-792753","identifier":[{"id":"85188738473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-003f419e-aac5-42bf-a1cb-1ed5eb610b85","itu-a8d5ba0b-f96c-4003-90c6-b851b67088aa"],"keyword":["citation analysis","impact","interactive information retrieval","re-use","sharing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C3D4E0F2B40A18F936F1310EDFAD8EAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/743728581/3627508.3638338.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3627508.3638338","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"open university milton keynes","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Open University Milton Keynes","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"the open university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Open University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Humanomics Research Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Responsible Impact","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gaedepau","last":"Gaede","name":"Gaede, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"e726f512-d3fd-4d89-962a-3aa9f532a52f","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Michael","key":"hallpau","last":"Hall","name":"Hall, Mark Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3627508.3638338","eisbn":["9798400704345"],"pages":"34-44","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"CHIIR 2024 - Proceedings of the 2024 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85188738473"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-003f419e-aac5-42bf-a1cb-1ed5eb610b85","itu-a8d5ba0b-f96c-4003-90c6-b851b67088aa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Impact of CHIIR Publications : A Study of Eight Years of CHIIR","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.72-792753","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Multistakeholder recommender systems are defined by [1] as those that account for “the preferences of multiple parties when generating recommendations, especially when these parties are on different sides of the recommendation interaction.” Due to their complexity, evaluating these systems cannot be restricted to the overall utility of a single stakeholder, as is often the case of more mainstream recommender system applications. In this section, we focus our discussion on the intricacies involved in understanding what is the “right” construct required to ensure the proper evaluation of multistakeholder recommender systems. We bring attention to the different aspects involved in the evaluation of multistakeholder recommender systems – from the range of stakeholders involved (beyond producers and consumers) to the values and specific goals of each relevant stakeholder. Additionally, we discuss how to move from theoretical evaluation to practical implementation, providing specific use case examples. Finally, we outline open research directions for the RecSys community to explore. Our aim in this section is to provide guidance to researchers and practitioners about how to think about these complex and domain-dependent issues in the course of designing, developing, and researching applications with multistakeholder aspects.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Burke, Robin","Adomavicius, Gediminas","Bogers, Toine","Di Noia, Tomasso","Kowald, Dominik","Neidhardt, Julia","Özgöbek, Özlem","Pera, Maria","Ziegler, Jürgen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789568"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Know-Center Graz","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Polytechnic University of Bari","Technische Universität Graz","University of Colorado","University of Duisburg-Essen","University of Minnesota","Vienna University of Technology"],"keyword":["Evaluation","Information retrieval","Intelligent Systems","Multi Stakeholder Processes","Recommender systems","User interaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multistakeholder and multimethod evaluation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/DagRep.14.5.58","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789568","ids":["itu-b077f33c-c308-407b-b4fe-6a2ee2336dfe"],"keyword":["Evaluation","Information Retrieval","Intelligent Systems","Multi-Stakeholder Processes","Recommender Systems","User Interaction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2163AB4650536AE519B30BBC7F311A90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/DagRep.14.5.58","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of colorado","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Colorado","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of minnesota","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Minnesota","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, NEtwoRks, Data, and Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of bari","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Bari","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"at","key":"know center graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Know-Center Graz","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"at","key":"technische universität graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technische Universität Graz","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"at","key":"vienna university of technology","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Vienna University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"de","key":"university of duisburg essen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Duisburg-Essen","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"burkepau","last":"Burke","name":"Burke, Robin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gediminas","key":"adomaviciuspau","last":"Adomavicius","name":"Adomavicius, Gediminas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"e726f512-d3fd-4d89-962a-3aa9f532a52f","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasso","key":"dinoiapau","last":"Di Noia","name":"Di Noia, Tomasso","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominik","key":"kowaldpau","last":"Kowald","name":"Kowald, Dominik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia","key":"neidhardtpau","last":"Neidhardt","name":"Neidhardt, Julia","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Özlem","key":"özgöbekpau","last":"Özgöbek","name":"Özgöbek, Özlem","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"perapau","last":"Pera","name":"Pera, Maria","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Jürgen","key":"zieglerpau","last":"Ziegler","name":"Ziegler, Jürgen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18624405"],"issue":"5","pages":"123-145","place":"Dagstuhl","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","series":"Dagstuhl Seminar Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Evaluation Perspectives of Recommender Systems: Driving Research and Education (Dagstuhl Seminar 24211)","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b077f33c-c308-407b-b4fe-6a2ee2336dfe"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Multistakeholder and Multimethod Evaluation","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789568","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"While the rise of online job portals and corporate websites have allowed for easier collection of digital candidate CVs, much of the candidate identification and assessment process—also known as talent search—still requires manual work from recruiters. Recruitment is a professional search domain that has been largely overlooked in IR research, even though better support of recruiters in finding more high-quality candidates could have a big impact on job seekers, companies and society as a whole. Such recruiter support can only be built on top of a more thorough understanding of the information seeking behavior of recruiters when trying to identify the most relevant candidates for open job postings. In this paper, we present the results of a log-based study of the information seeking process of recruiters at one of Scandinavia’s largest job portals and recruitment agencies. We analyze the behavior of recruiters at different search stages according to the model by Vakkari [24] and distinguish between different types of recruitment tasks. In addition, we contextualize the results of our log analysis using the findings from earlier conducted contextual inquiries to help explain our findings. Our results show that both matching and recruiting talent search is a complex task: recruiters usually submit multiple queries during sessions that can last for hours. We also find that the search behaviour of recruiters during a recruitment task changes over time: recruiters tend to use more filters, formulate longer and more diverse queries, and spend more time assessing candidates near the end of a session than in the beginning. We also observe some differences in search behavior between the different recruitment tasks.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kaya, Mesut","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095837"],"event":{"end":"2023-03-23","place":"Austin, us","start":"2023-03-19","title":"CHIIR '23: ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["HR","Information seeking","Professional search","Recruitment","query log analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"understanding recruiters information seeking behavior in talent search","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85151477500&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-095837","identifier":[{"id":"85151477500","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9de60c22-c059-4d3d-9172-b1d39343ef12"],"keyword":["HR","Recruitment","information seeking","professional search","query log analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6FFF1903DD7E89E36B3D14D1739AAAF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesut","key":"kayapau","last":"Kaya","locid":"3fa53166-7b51-4879-9492-255eac2a2793","name":"Kaya, Mesut","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","name":"Bogers, Toine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3576840.3578311","eisbn":["9798400700354"],"pages":"14-23","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"CHIIR 2023 - Proceedings of the 2023 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151477500"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9de60c22-c059-4d3d-9172-b1d39343ef12"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Understanding Recruiters’ Information Seeking Behavior in Talent Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-095837","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We studied the collaboration patterns of CHIIR authors, and found that most papers are collaborative. A core of 33% of the CHIIR researchers are directly connected and frequently co-author, and several disconnected clusters also make frequent CHIIR contributions. We also studied citation impact of the CHIIR papers and show that in relation to research design type, theoretical and empirical papers tend to receive more citations than resource papers. With regards to sharing and re-use, papers that share at least one resource tend to have significantly higher citation impact - in particular when sharing data resources and design resources. Re-using resources does not significantly increase citation impact in itself.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Larsen, Birger","Koolen, Marijn","Gäde, Maria","Hall, Mark M.","Petras, Vivien"],"cuid":["S02-087.44-724283"],"event":{"end":"2023-03-23","place":"Austin, us","start":"2023-03-19","title":"8th ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Huygens Institute for the History of the Netherlands","Open University Milton Keynes","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","The Open University"],"keyword":["CHIIR","Citation impact","Collaboration","data sharing and re use"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collaboration patterns and impact of sharing at chiir","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft