iation for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"CHIIR 2023 - Proceedings of the 2023 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","status":"p","title":"CHIIR 2023 - Proceedings of the 2023 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151425549"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a0837b68-78cb-4e4b-b071-3998f9c6cf5c","itu-36df53ec-58f5-432b-830b-4c1d8b5303fa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Collaboration Patterns and Impact of Sharing at CHIIR","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.44-724283","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present the results of an initial study of the research, sharing, and re-use practices at the CHIIR conference through a systematic analysis of all CHIIR papers published from 2016 to 2022. We find that CHIIR is a conference predominantly focused on empirical, multi-methods research that over the years has undergone a focusing in terms of the type of research methods that are being used. A modest number of papers re-use existing data and design resources, but infrastructure component re-use is much more rare. Only a fraction of CHIIR papers actually share their own resources, which suggests that there is much to gain in terms of reproducibility of research presented at CHIIR and could potentially be used to support changes in reviewing practices.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Hall, Mark Michael","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Larsen, Birger"],"cuid":["S02-088.46-715770"],"event":{"end":"2023-03-23","place":"Austin, us","start":"2023-03-19","title":"8th ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Huygens Institute for the History of the Netherlands","Open University Milton Keynes","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","The Open University"],"keyword":["Interactive information retrieval","Re use","Sharing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how we work share and re use at chiir","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"