:"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","name_org":"Meier, Florian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3498366.3505798","eisbn":["9781450391863"],"pages":"371-373","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of CHIIR '22: ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127448742"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fc589498-0742-4311-8438-03c384667ff0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Information Quality in Information Interaction and Retrieval: Workshop Proposal for CHIIR 2022","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123328","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"With ever-increasing amounts of complex data, we need compelling ways to distill this information into meaningful, memorable and engaging insights. Data storytelling is an emerging visualization paradigm that aims to “tell a story” with data in order to elicit deeper reflections in an effective manner. However, the effects of adding a narrative to a visualization on the memorability of the information remain speculative. Based on a review of related work, we synthesize a framework of data storytelling principles with concrete actions for every principle. We use this framework to design an online, controlled experiment to test compare traditional data visualizations with data storytelling visualizations in terms of their effects on short-term and long-term recall of information displayed in the visualizations. In general, despite long-held assumptions in the visualization community, we find no significant differences in recall between traditional visualizations and data storytelling visualization. However, we find indications that the cognitive load induced by different chart types and self-assessed prior knowledge on the chart topics could possibly have a moderating effect on information recall.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Zdanovic, Dominyk","Lembcke, Tanja Julie","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063026"],"event":{"end":"2022-03-18","place":"Virtual, Online, de","start":"2022-03-14","title":"7th ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data storytelling","Data visualization","Information interaction","Learning effect","Memory","Recall"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the influence of data storytelling on the ability to recall information","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3498366.3505755","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-063026","identifier":[{"id":"85127391112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2cbeab85-b765-4151-ab17-e0e0a7f4cb60"],"keyword":["Data storytelling","data visualization","information interaction","learning effect","memory","recall"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-548C851A8B79BC26E8355AB65FE5C42B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3498366.3505755","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517547379/3498366.3505755.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dominyk","key":"zdanovicpau","last":"Zdanovic","name":"Zdanovic, Dominyk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tanja Julie","key":"lembckepau","last":"Lembcke","locid":"12ca7e60-3580-45fa-8b90-02d8cefe6218","name":"Lembcke, Tanja Julie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3498366.3505755","eisbn":["9781450391863"],"pages":"67-77","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"CHIIR 2022 - Proceedings of the 2022 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","status":"p","subtitle":"CHIIR '22","title":"Proceedings of the 2022 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127391112"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2cbeab85-b765-4151-ab17-e0e0a7f4cb60"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Influence of Data Storytelling on the Ability to Recall Information","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063026","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Query-level evaluation metrics such as nDCG that originate from field of Information Retrieval (IR) have seen widespread adoption in the Recommender Systems (RS) community for comparing the quality of different ranked lists of recommendations with different levels of relevance to the user. However, the traditional (offline) RS evaluation paradigm is typically restricted to evaluating a single results list. In contrast, IR researchers have also developed evaluation metrics over the past decade for the session-based evaluation of more complex search tasks. Here, the sessions consist of multiple queries and multi-round search interactions, and the metrics evaluate the quality of the session as a whole. Despite the popularity of the more traditional single-list evaluation paradigm, RS can also be used to assist users with complex information access tasks. In this paper, we explore the usefulness of session-level evaluation metrics for evaluating and comparing the performance of both recommender systems and search engines. We show that, despite possible misconceptions that comparing both scenarios is akin to comparing apples to oranges, it is indeed possible to compare recommendation results from a single ranked list to the results from a whole search session. In doing so, we address the following questions: (1) how can we fairly and realistically compare the quality of an individual list of recommended items to the quality of an entire manual search session; (2) how can we measure the contribution that the RS is making to the entire search session. We contextualize our claims by focusing on a particular complex search scenario: the problem of talent search. An example of professional search, talent search involves recruiters searching for relevant candidates given a specific job posting by issuing multiple queries in the course of a search session. We show that it is possible to compare the search behavior and success of recruiters to that of a matchmaking recommender system that generates a single ranked list of relevant candidates for a given job posting. In particular, we adopt a session-based metric from IR and motivate how it can be used to perform valid and realistic comparisons of recommendation lists to multiple-query search sessions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kaya, Mesut","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-085058"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-22","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2022-09-22","title":"2022 Perspectives on the Evaluation of Recommender Systems Workshop, PERSPECTIVES 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kaya, Mesut"],"keyword":["Evaluation","Job recommendation","Recruitment","SEARCH"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards comparing recommendation to multiple query search sessions for talent search","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517887376/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by the Innovation Fund Denmark, grant no. 0175-000005B."],"id":"S01-000.00-085058","identifier":[{"id":"85140338925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-788d7f39-41ca-4fb6-9c67-167015727e61"],"keyword":["evaluation","job recommendation","recruitment","search","session-based recommendation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C1086058E247D8A4970351EF730771C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/517887376/Open_Access_Article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3228/paper6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesut","key":"kayapau","last":"Kaya","locid":"3fa53166-7b51-4879-9492-255eac2a2793","name":"Kaya, Mesut","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","paperid":"6","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"3228"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140338925"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-788d7f39-41ca-4fb6-9c67-167015727e61"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Towards Comparing Recommendation to Multiple-Query Search Sessions for Talent Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https