{"abstract":"For the task of job recommendations, common practice is to recommend job postings to job seekers, and recently different embedding techniques have been applied to solve this task. A common way to represent job seekers and job postings as embeddings is to use the whole textual data of the job postings and job seekers' resumes. Instead of using the whole textual data, textual data source like job title, knowledge, skills, abilities can be used as well. In this work, we present findings of a preliminary offline study, where we explore the impact of utilizing different types of embeddings to recommend job seekers to given job postings, unlike the common practice of recommending job postings to job seekers. We explore the effectiveness of using job title based embeddings compared with the embeddings based on resume and job posting full-text descriptions. Using a dataset from JobIndex -Scandinavia's largest job portals and recruitment agencies- our experimental results show that representing job seekers and job postings as embeddings by using job title text only can be at least as informative as using the full-text descriptions for most of the cases.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kaya, Mesut","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-052094"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-01","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2021-09-27","title":"2021 Workshop on Recommender Systems for Human Resources, RECSYS IN HR 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["E Recruitment","Embeddings","HR","Job matching","Job recommendation","Recruitment"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of job title based embeddings on résumé to job ad recommendation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/464971521/Kaya_Bogers.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by the Innovation Fund Denmark, grant no. 0175-000005B."],"id":"S01-000.00-052094","identifier":[{"id":"85116890702","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-072469df-766d-4045-8041-aa9ee2b676db"],"keyword":["HR","e-recruitment","embeddings","job matching","job recommendation","recruitment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-B1F702F03F18ED84D410416CBCA01CAC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/464971521/Kaya_Bogers.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2967/","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human-centered AI","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesut","key":"kayapau","last":"Kaya","locid":"3fa53166-7b51-4879-9492-255eac2a2793","name":"Kaya, Mesut","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"2967"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116890702"],"sdg":["8. Decent Work and Economic Growth","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-072469df-766d-4045-8041-aa9ee2b676db"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Effectiveness of job title based embeddings on résumé to job ad recommendation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-052094","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This perspective paper on resource re-use intends to draw the attention of the interactive information retrieval (IIR) community to the challenges of research documentation and archiving for future use. Resources are understood as encompassing research designs, research data and research infrastructures. It proposes eight principles for improving the re-use of resources in the IIR community and presents concrete steps on how to achieve them. A five-level system for data archiving and documentation envisions increasingly open and stable documentation and access infrastructures.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gäde, Maria","Koolen, Marijn","Hall, Mark","Bogers, Toine","Petras, Vivien"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-084564"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2021-03-19","place":"Canberra, au","start":"2021-03-15","title":"6th ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Open University Milton Keynes","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences"],"keyword":["Re use","Research Data","Research Design","Research Software","data documentation","data sharing practices"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a manifesto on resource re use in interactive information retrieval","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3406522.3446056","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-084564","identifier":[{"id":"85102725984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-76ded0c