{"abstract":"We explore the information seeking behaviour of the recruiters while they search to find candidate job seekers that match the open positions posted by the organizations. We perform a set of contextual inquiries with recruiters at one of Scandinavia's largest job portals and recruitment agencies by using its job database system. We aim to better understand short-term (matching) and long-term (recruitment) information seeking behaviour of the recruiters and their interaction with the search engine based on Solr. Based on the conducted contextual inquiries, we list a set of design implications to be used for better matching systems that can assist the recruiters to find more relevant candidates.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Kaya, Mesut"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061870"],"event":{"end":"2021-10-01","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2021-09-27","title":"2021 Workshop on Recommender Systems for Human Resources, RECSYS IN HR 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["HR","Information seeking","Job recommendation","Professional search","Recruitment"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an exploration of the information seeking behavior of recruiters","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/464968648/An_exploration_of_the_information_seeking_behavior_of_recruiters.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was supported by the Innovation Fund Denmark, grant no. 0175-000005B. We thank Qiuchi Li for his contributions during the contextual inquiries. We also thank the Jobindex recruiters who participated in our contextual inquiries."],"id":"S01-000.00-061870","identifier":[{"id":"85116866000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-28cae1b8-52a2-43a2-b170-30d198150eac"],"keyword":["HR","information seeking","job recommendation","professional search","recruitment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-65737C473FC479026FD9997B15EB0765"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/464968648/An_exploration_of_the_information_seeking_behavior_of_recruiters.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2967/","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human-centered AI","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mesut","key":"kayapau","last":"Kaya","locid":"3fa53166-7b51-4879-9492-255eac2a2793","name":"Kaya, Mesut","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","pages":"11-18","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"2967"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116866000"],"sdg":["8. Decent Work and Economic Growth","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-28cae1b8-52a2-43a2-b170-30d198150eac"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An exploration of the information seeking behavior of recruiters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061870","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"During the past decade, recommender systems have rapidly become an indispensable element of websites, apps, and other platforms that seek to provide personalized interactions to their users. As recommendation technologies are applied to an ever-growing array of non-standard problems and scenarios, researchers and practitioners are also increasingly faced with challenges of dealing with greater variety and complexity in the inputs to those recommender systems. For example, there has been more reliance on fine-grained user signals as inputs rather than simple ratings or likes. Applications require more complex domain-specific constraints on inputs to the recommender systems. Likewise, the outputs of recommender systems are moving towards more complex composite items, such as package or sequence recommendations. This increasing complexity requires smarter recommender algorithms that can deal with this diversity in inputs and outputs. For the past four years, the ComplexRec workshop series has offered an interactive venue for discussing approaches to recommendation in complex scenarios that have no simple one-size-fits-all solution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Abdollahpouri, Himan","Bogers, Toine","Mobasher, Bamshad","Petersen, Casper","Pera, Maria Soledad Soledad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-083650"],"event":{"acronym":"RecSys","end":"2021-10-01","place":"Virtual, Online, nl","start":"2021-09-27","title":"15th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems, RecSys 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boise State University","DePaul University","Northwestern University"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation","Recommender systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexrec 000000002021 fifth workshop on recommendation in complex environments","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85115648774&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-083650","identifier":[{"id":"85115648774","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7397b799-877c-41d8-a4dc-0ca63f4f24d3"],"keyword":["complex recommendation","recommender systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B880E471D3F48EC4E35BEF317475F30E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"northwestern university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Northwestern University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"depaul university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DePaul University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["SamPension A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"boise state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Boise State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Himan","key":"abdollahpouripau","last":"Abdollahpouri","name":"Abdollahpouri, Himan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bamshad","key":"mobasherpau","last":"Mobasher","name":"Mobasher, Bamshad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Casper","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Soledad Soledad","key":"perapau","last":"Pera","name":"Pera, Maria Soledad Soledad","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3460231.3470928","eisbn":["9781450384582"],"pages":"775-777","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"RecSys 2021 - 15th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems","status":"p","title":"RecSys 2021 - 15th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115648774"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","sampension a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7397b799-877c-41d8-a4dc-0ca63f4f24d3"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"ComplexRec 2021 : Fifth workshop on recommendation in complex environments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-083650","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"With the advent of the retro-gaming movement there is an increasing interest in rediscovering games once played. Tip of my Joystick' is a Reddit community dedicated to the re-finding of forgotten games. In this subreddit, users describe games they wish to re-find so that other users may help them identify the game's title. This community thus offers a unique opportunity for studying how players recall and describe games and play experiences of the past. This paper presents the results of an analysis of a random sample of 250 posts from this subreddit. The posts were analyzed in terms of what aspects of games they describe For the purpose of this analysis we developed a coding scheme consisting of 38 individual codes belonging to 9 different main categories. Our findings may contribute to research on game archiving and collection as they may help inform the design of better game search engines.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-065642"],"event":{"acronym":"FGD(?)","end":"2020-09-18","place":"Bugibba, mt","start":"2020-09-15","title":"15th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games, FDG 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Re finding","Video games","complex information needs","game archives","game description","known item search"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kinda like the sims but with ghosts a qualitative analysis of video game re finding requests on reddit","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-065642","identifier":[{"id":"85092276457","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-35b1c44b-b8ea-4f1e-8f35-3ecffda2db53"],"keyword":["complex information needs","game archives","game description","known-item search","re-finding","video games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-E2762C749EDD3AAF310416A4C6E3175F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Ida Kathrine Hammeleff","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Georgios N.","key":"yannakakispedh","last":"Yannakakis","name":"Yannakakis, Georgios N.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonios","key":"liapispedh","last":"Liapis","name":"Liapis, Antonios","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kyburz","key":"pennypedh","last":"Penny","name":"Penny, Kyburz","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Vanessa","key":"volzpedh","last":"Volz","name":"Volz, Vanessa","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Foaad","key":"khosmoodpedh","last":"Khosmood","name":"Khosmood, Foaad","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Phil","key":"lopespedh","last":"Lopes","name":"Lopes, Phil","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3402942.3402971","eisbn":["9781450388078"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"ACM International Conference Proceeding Series","status":"p","title":"FDG '20: Proceedings of the 15th International Conference on the Foundations of Digital Games"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092276457"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-35b1c44b-b8ea-4f1e-8f35-3ecffda2db53"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"Kinda like the Sims... but with ghosts?\": A Qualitative Analysis of Video Game Re-finding Requests on Reddit","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-065642","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Distractions while driving are a major cause of traffic accidents and chief among these is the use of mobile phones. Driver distractions typically fall into four categories-visual, cognitive, bio-mechanical, and auditory-and different technological solutions have been proposed to address these. Intelligent Personal Assistants (IPAs), such as Siri, is a recent example of such a technological solution that offers the potential for hands-free phone interaction through a voice-controlled interface. IPAs could potentially reduce visual and bio-mechanical distractions if they are usable enough to not increase a driver's cognitive load. We present the results of a controlled experiment with the aim of understanding how the use of Siri while driving compares to manual interaction in terms of usability and distractions. We also tested these two interaction types in the lab in order to understand how the main driving task influences Siri's (perceived) usability. Our study shows that Siri is not ready for every-day use in the car: interacting with Siri while driving is likely to be unsafe for most participants, especially less experienced drivers. Participants were distracted by Siri due to its over-reliance on visual feedback as well as frequent time-outs by Siri when waiting for a response from a driver occupied with the road environment. Speech recognition quality in a noisy car as well as problematic multi-lingual speech recognition in general are other issues that resulted in low usability and more cognitive distractions. While interacting with Siri may be hands-free, it does not provide an eyes-free and distraction-free experience yet.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Helene Høgh","Scheel, Alexander Nuka","Bogers, Toine","Larsen, Birger"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053860"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2020-03-18","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2020-03-14","title":"5th ACM SIGIR Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Helene Høgh"],"keyword":["Driving","IPA","Intelligent Personal Assistants","Siri","Usability testing"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hands free but not eyes free a usability evaluation of siri while driving","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-053860","identifier":[{"id":"85082486940","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0d096891-6773-4968-91cd-0521b4328b4b"],"keyword":["Driving","Intelligent personal assistants","Ipa","Siri","Usability testing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A0BDBD871D0938AE2E081F3FADD05CA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helene Høgh","key":"larsenhelenehøghpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Helene Høgh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander Nuka","key":"scheelalexandernukapau","last":"Scheel","name":"Scheel, Alexander Nuka","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerstoinepau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenbirgerpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3343413.3377962","eisbn":["9781450368926"],"pages":"63-72","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"CHIIR 2020 - Proceedings of the 2020 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval","status":"p","title":"CHIIR '20: Proceedings of the 2020 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082486940"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0d096891-6773-4968-91cd-0521b4328b4b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Hands-free but not Eyes-free : A Usability Evaluation of Siri while Driving","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053860","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"During the past decade, recommender systems have rapidly become an indispensable element of websites, apps, and other platforms that are looking to provide personalized interaction to their users. As recommendation technologies are applied to an ever-growing array of non-standard problems and scenarios, researchers and practitioners are also increasingly faced with challenges of dealing with greater variety and complexity in the inputs to those recommender systems. For example, there has been more reliance on fine-grained user signals as inputs rather than simple ratings or likes. Many applications also require more complex domain-specific constraints on inputs to the recommender systems. The outputs of recommender systems are also moving towards more complex composite items, such as package or sequence recommendations. This increasing complexity requires smarter recommender algorithms that can deal with this diversity in inputs and outputs. The ComplexRec workshop series offers an interactive venue for discussing approaches to recommendation in complex scenarios that have no simple one-size-fits-all solution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Koolen, Marijn","Petersen, Casper","Mobasher, Bamshad","Tuzhilin, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-122414"],"event":{"acronym":"RecSys","end":"2020-09-26","place":"Virtual, Online, br","start":"2020-09-22","title":"14th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems, RecSys 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DePaul University","New York University","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation","Recommender systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexrec 000000002020 workshop on recommendation in complex environments","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-122414","identifier":[{"id":"85092733188","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f91b49fc-ffff-41ea-be43-293d0d852f8a"],"keyword":["complex recommendation","recommender systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E4B7EC550320D37BFBD9D3E27FDA9CE4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Sampension"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"depaul university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":