{"abstract":"With the rapid growth of the video game industry over the past decade, there has been a commensurate increase in research activity focused on a variety of aspects of video games. How people discover the video games they want to play and how they articulate these information needs is still largely unknown, however. A better understanding of video game-related information needs and what makes a game relevant to a user could aid in the design of more effective, domain-specific search engines. In this paper we take a first step towards such domain-specific understanding. We present an analysis of a random sample of 521 complex game requests posted on Reddit. A coding scheme was developed that captures the 41 different aspects of relevance and information needs expressed in these requests. We find that game requests contain an average of close to 5 different relevance aspects. Several of these relevance aspects are geared specifically to video games, while others are more general.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Skov, Mette"],"cuid":["S02-080.00-715693"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2019-04-03","place":"Washington, us","start":"2019-03-31","title":"14th International Conference on Information in Contemporary Society, iConference 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bogers, Toine"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences"],"keyword":["Complex search","Game search","Information need categorization","Query analysis","Relevance aspects","Video games"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"looking for an amazing game i can relax and sink hours into a study of relevance aspects in video game discovery","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85064058307&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-080.00-715693","identifier":[{"id":"85064058307","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-75607bce-cfec-477a-8fe2-1faad01d3888","itu-d29e9dd8-66af-447b-b34d-834b966dce7d"],"keyword":["Complex search","Game search","Information need categorization","Query analysis","Relevance aspects","Video games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5743F2C03270ADC3167667E7BCC3D461"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Natalie Greene","key":"taylorpedh","last":"Taylor","name":"Taylor, Natalie Greene","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Caitlin","key":"christianlambpedh","last":"Christian-Lamb","name":"Christian-Lamb, Caitlin","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michelle H.","key":"martinpedh","last":"Martin","name":"Martin, Michelle H.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bonnie","key":"nardipedh","last":"Nardi","name":"Nardi, Bonnie","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-15742-5_48","eisbn":["9783030157425"],"isbn":["9783030157418"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"503-515","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"14th International Conference, iConference 2019, Proceedings","title":"Information in Contemporary Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064058307"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-75607bce-cfec-477a-8fe2-1faad01d3888","itu-d29e9dd8-66af-447b-b34d-834b966dce7d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"“Looking for an Amazing Game I Can Relax and Sink Hours into..” : A Study of Relevance Aspects in Video Game Discovery","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.00-715693","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Over the past decade, recommendation algorithms for ratings prediction and item ranking have steadily matured. However, these state-of-the-art algorithms are typically applied in relatively straightforward and static scenarios: given information about a user's past item preferences in isolation, can we predict whether they will like a new item or rank all unseen items based on predicted interest? In reality, recommendation is often a more complex problem: the evaluation of a list of recommended items never takes place in a vacuum, and it is often a single step in the user's more complex background task or need. The goal of the ComplexRec 2019 workshop is to ofer an interactive venue for discussing approaches to recommendation in complex scenarios that have no simple one-size-fts-all solution.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Koolen, Marijn","Bogers, Toine","Mobasher, Bamshad","Tuzhilin, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-064133"],"event":{"acronym":"RecSys","end":"2019-09-20","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-09-16","title":"13th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems, RecSys 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DePaul University","Humanities Cluster Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","New York University"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"third workshop on recommendation in complex scenarios complexrec 000000002019","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85073317959&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-064133","identifier":[{"id":"85073317959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-30aed6dd-65c0-4b95-8a09-c2ef3803ad8c"],"keyword":["complex recommendation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87ACBCC054876DF26B5A46DFDFE0F306"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"humanities cluster royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humanities Cluster Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"depaul university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DePaul University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bamshad","key":"mobasherpau","last":"Mobasher","name":"Mobasher, Bamshad","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"tuzhilinpau","last":"Tuzhilin","name":"Tuzhilin, Alexander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3298689.3346948","eisbn":["9781450362436"],"pages":"550-551","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"RecSys 2019 - 13th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073317959"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-30aed6dd-65c0-4b95-8a09-c2ef3803ad8c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Third workshop on recommendation in complex scenarios (ComplexreC 2019)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-064133","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Context-aware recommender systems consider contextual features as additional information to predict user's preferences. For example, the recommendations could be based on time, location, or the company of other people. Among the contextual information, time became an important feature because user preferences tend to change over time or be similar in the near future. Researchers have proposed diferent models to incorporate time into their recommender system, however, the current models are not able to capture specifc temporal patterns. To address the limitation observed in previous works, we propose Collective embedding for Neural Context-Aware Recommender Systems (CoNCARS). The proposed solution jointly model the item, user and time embeddings to capture temporal patterns. Then, CoNCARS use the outer product to model the user-item-time correlations between dimensions of the embedding space. The hidden features feed our Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) to learn the non-linearities between the diferent features. Finally, we combine the output from our CNNs in the fusion layer and then predict the user's preference score. We conduct extensive experiments on real-world datasets, demonstrating CoNCARS improves the top-N item recommendation task and outperform the state-of-the-art recommendation methods.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Da Costa, Felipe Soares","Dolog, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123803"],"event":{"acronym":"RecSys","end":"2018-09-20","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2018-09-16","title":"RecSys 2019: 13th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Convolutional neural networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collective embedding for neural context aware recommender systems","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-123803","identifier":[{"id":"85073340225","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fe0f119a-2dd2-4e9a-975b-3f17963904cd"],"keyword":["Collective Embedding","Context-aware Recommender Systems","Convolutional Neural Networks","Time-aware Recommendations"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F8D914191A4459A35F6DB348C6FBB95"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Database, Programming and Web Technologies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Felipe Soares Da","key":"costapau","last":"Costa","locid":"b47a628f-f7a7-4b5c-9f0e-47e1a7969d8e","name":"Da Costa, Felipe Soares","name_org":"Costa, Felipe Soares Da","orcid":"0000-0002-5862-2318","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dologpau","last":"Dolog","locid":"8dca6359-9ed2-4b65-8bcf-714003a9b1ff","name":"Dolog, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-1842-9131","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspedh","last":"Bogers","name":"Bogers, Toine","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alan","key":"saidpedh","last":"Said","name":"Said, Alan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"brusilovskypedh","last":"Brusilovsky","name":"Brusilovsky, Peter","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Domonkos","key":"tikkpedh","last":"Tikk","name":"Tikk, Domonkos","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3298689.3347028","eisbn":["9781450362436"],"isbn":["9781450362436"],"pages":"201-209","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems, RecSys 2019, Copenhagen, Denmark, September 16-20, 2019."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85073340225"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fe0f119a-2dd2-4e9a-975b-3f17963904cd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Collective embedding for neural context-aware recommender systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123803","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"A preliminary review of 145 IIiX and CHIIR papers on experimental IIR studies was performed in order to identify elements of the methodological approach of IIR studies, which are important to document for later access and re-use. The papers’ ACM publication metadata was also analyzed for reporting methodological details. The analysis suggests 17 reporting elements and finds that current metadata practices are not sufficient documentation for this purpose.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Petras, Vivien","Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-123927"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2019-03-14","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2019-03-14","title":"2019 CHIIR Workshop on Barriers to Interactive IR Resources Re-use, BIIRRR 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Interactive IR","Meta review","Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"elements of iir studies a review of the 000000002006 000000002018 iiix and chiir conferences","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/330025359/paper6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-123927","identifier":[{"id":"85063442323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-fe8d42db-e467-43a2-aef8-33d4d868e5aa"],"keyword":["CHIIR conferences","Content metadata analyis","IIiX","Interactive IR","Meta review","Methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C1B3039FFD8B82D47283541855D28AE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/330025359/paper6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","pages":"37-41","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"2337"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063442323"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fe8d42db-e467-43a2-aef8-33d4d868e5aa"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Elements of IIR studies : A review of the 2006-2018 IIiX and CHIIR conferences","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-123927","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INEX ran as an independent evaluation forum for 10 years before it teamed up with CLEF in 2012. Even before 2012 there was considerable collaboration between INEX and CLEF, and these collaborations increased in intensity when CLEF moved beyond its traditional cross-lingual focus in 2009/2010 shifting to include all experimental IR. This led to the merger of CLEF and INEX, and effectively to the inclusion of INEX as a large track or lab into CLEF in 2012. This chapter details the efforts of the INEX lab in CLEF (2012–2014), as well as the ongoing activities as separate labs, under the labels Social Book Search (2015–2016), and Microblog Contextualization (2016–2018).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jaap, Kamps","Koolen, Marijn","Geva, Shlomo","Schenkel, Ralf","SanJuan, Eric","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-087556"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Trier University","University of Amsterdam"],"keyword":["CLEF","Information retrieval","LibraryThing","Social book search","XML retrieval"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from xml retrieval to semantic search and beyond the inex sbs and mc000000000002 labs of clef 000000002012 000000002018","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9783030229474","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-087556","ids":["aau-80fe2ee6-ee02-4c27-a488-b4c4744e4cc7"],"keyword":["LibraryThing","clef","inex","information retrieval","social book search","xml retrieval"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1EE