le":"Information in Contemporary Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064058193"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d7cef94e-eabc-4400-be7d-ac157180b6b6","itu-7e5e8ea4-9d1c-434f-ae7c-0076d2943cf8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Study of Usage and Usability of Intelligent Personal Assistants in Denmark","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.14-715788","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The goal of the BIIRRR 2018 workshop is to serve as a starting point for a community-driven effort to design and implement a platform for the collection, organization, maintenance, and sharing of resources for interactive information retrieval (IIR) experimentation. Examples include search tasks, experimental protocols, questionnaire designs, reporting standards, evaluation procedures, data collections, and the search interaction data produced in such experiments. The goal of the BIIRRR 2018 workshop [2] was to serve as a starting point for a community-driven effort to design and implement a platform for the collection, organization, maintenance, and sharing of resources for interactive information retrieval (IIR) experimentation.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Hall, Mark","Freund, Luanne","Koolen, Marijn","Petras, Vivien","Skov, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-078873"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2018-03-15","place":"New Brunswick, us","start":"2018-03-11","title":"CHIIR 2018: 3rd ACM SIGIR Conference on Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin","Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","University of British Columbia"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"report on the workshop on barriers to interactive ir resources re use biirrr 000000002018","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sigir.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/p119.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-078873","ids":["aau-634697ff-a2cc-409e-875c-01bd06f3d453"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-473A81761EB8F90E04D5BB00F160B480"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sigir.org/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/p119.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"martin luther university halle wittenberg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Martin Luther University Halle-Wittenberg","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"hallpau","last":"Hall","name":"Hall, Mark","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luanne","key":"freundpau","last":"Freund","name":"Freund, Luanne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01635840"],"pages":"119-128","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"SIGIR Forum","status":"p","title":"SIGIR Forum"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-634697ff-a2cc-409e-875c-01bd06f3d453"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Report on the Workshop on Barriers to Interactive IR Resources Re-use (BIIRRR 2018)","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-078873","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"While ownership and usage of handheld devices such as smartphones and tablets continues to grow at a rapid pace, we do not have complete picture of how people manage personal information on these devices. The few existing studies have typically used interview or survey methods to focus on personal information management (PIM) practices on smartphones. We present the results of an exploratory contextual inquiry study of PIM practices aimed at providing a structured, naturalistic overview of PIM on both smartphones and tablets. We find that people use multiple complementary strategies to acquire different types of information on their devices, and that people rely strongly on automatic chronological ordering instead of organization by subject, although this pays off most for smaller information collections. Deletion of information is strongly influenced by usefulness and personal attachment. Finally, we find that people strongly prefer browsing over search when retrieving information from their devices.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jensen, Amalie Enshelm","Jægerfelt, Caroline Møller","Francis, Sanne","Larsen, Birger","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-087886"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2018-03-15","place":"New Brunswick, us","start":"2018-03-11","title":"CHIIR 2018: 3rd ACM SIGIR Conference on Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i just scroll through my stuff until i find it or give up a contextual inquiry of pim on private handheld devices","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85050455978&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-087886","identifier":[{"id":"85050455978","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-821f744d-02ca-41b3-a18a-e51dd8a0dfa6"],"keyword":["information behavior, information organization, personal information management, smartphones, tablets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ED2DF0371B02589D0A43D704D042929D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Responsible Impact","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Amalie Enshelm","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Amalie Enshelm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Møller","key":"jægerfeltpau","last":"Jægerfelt","name":"Jægerfelt, Caroline Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne","key":"francispau","last":"Francis","name":"Francis, Sanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9cb12135-a825-43ba-87e2-b71651b91939","name":"Larsen, Birger","orcid":"0000-0002-3622-2698","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3176349.3176394","isbn":["9781450349253"],"pages":"140-149","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"CHIIR '18","status":"p","title":"CHIIR 2018 - Proceedings of the 2018 Conference on Human Information Interaction and Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050455978"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-821f744d-02ca-41b3-a18a-e51dd8a0dfa6"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"I Just Scroll Through My Stuff Until I Find It or Give Up!\" : A Contextual Inquiry of PIM on Private Handheld Devices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-087886","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Social tagging is an information classification paradigm where the users themselves are given the power to describe and categorize content for their own purposes using tags. The popularity of social tagging, and the ease with which such tags can be generated, assigned, and collected, has sparked significant research interest in tags and their possible applications. One such application is tag-based recommendation: generating better recommendations by incorporating tags into the recommendation process. This chapter provides an overview of the state-of-the-art approaches to tag-based item recommendation, organised by the class of recommendation algorithms that is augmented with tags, such as collaborative filtering, dimensionality reduction, graph-based recommendation, content-based filtering, machine learning, and hybrid recommendation. The chapter also offers an overview of the most important methods for recommending which tags to apply to content. Finally, the chapter discusses the open research problems in tag-based recommendation and what would be needed to address them.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-061209"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Collaborative filtering","Machine learning","Recommender systems","Social tagging","Tag recommendation","content based recommendation","hybrid recommendation","social bookmarking","tag based recommendation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tag based recommendation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-061209","identifier":[{"id":"85046777137","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-266912de-a069-48ef-9e26-fa7539918f99"],"keyword":["collaborative filtering","content-based recommendation","hybrid recommendation","machine learning","recommender systems","social bookmarking","social tagging","tag recommendation","tag-based recommendation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-683E17C47AE133AA0A78B764BACA8701"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"brusilovskypedh","last":"Brusilovsky","name":"Brusilovsky, Peter","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daqing","key":"hepedh","last":"He","name":"He, Daqing","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-90092-6_12","eisbn":["9783319900926"],"isbn":["9783319900919"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"441-479","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Social Information Access"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046777137"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-266912de-a069-48ef-9e26-fa7539918f99"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Tag-Based Recommendation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061209","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Over the past decade, recommendation algorithms for ratings prediction and item ranking have steadily matured. However, these state-of-the-art algorithms are typically applied in relatively straightforward and static scenarios: given information about a user’s past item preferences in isolation, can we predict whether they will like a new item or rank all unseen items based on predicted interest? In reality, recommendation is often a more complex problem: the evaluation of a list of recommended items never takes place in a vacuum, and it is often a single step in the user’s more complex background task or need. The goal of the ComplexRec 2018 workshop is to offer an interactive venue for discussing approaches to recommendation in complex scenarios that have no simple one-size-fits-all solution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Petersen, Casper","Bogers, Toine","Koolen, Marijn","Mobasher, Bamshad","Said, Alan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063678"],"event":{"end":"2018-10-07","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2018-10-07","title":"ComplexRec 2018: 2nd Workshop on Recommendation in Complex Scenarios","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DePaul University","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","University of Skövde"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation","Recommender systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexrec 000000002018 proceedings of second workshop on recommendation in complex scenarios","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa