{"abstract":"Experimental evaluation carried out in international large-scale campaigns is a fundamental pillar of the scientific and technological advancement of information retrieval (IR) systems. Such evaluation activities produce a large quantity of scientific and experimental data, which are the foundation for all the subsequent scientific production and development of new systems. In this work, we discuss how to semantically annotate and interlink this data, with the goal of enhancing their interpretation, sharing, and reuse. We discuss the underlying evaluation workflow and propose a resource description framework model for those workflow parts. We use expertise retrieval as a case study to demonstrate the benefits of our semantic representation approach. We employ this model as a means for exposing experimental data as linked open data (LOD) on the Web and as a basis for enriching and automatically connecting this data with expertise topics and expert profiles. In this context, a topic-centric approach for expert search is proposed, addressing the extraction of expertise topics, their semantic grounding with the LOD cloud, and their connection to IR experimental data. Several methods for expert profiling and expert finding are analysed and evaluated. Our results show that it is possible to construct expert profiles starting from automatically extracted expertise topics and that topic-centric approaches outperform state-of-the-art language modelling approaches for expert finding.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Silvello, Gianmaria","Bordea, Georgeta","Ferro, Nicola","Buitelaar, Paul","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-082207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Silvello, Gianmaria"],"country":["Ireland","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Galway","University of Padua"],"keyword":["Experimental data","Resource description framework","Semantic enrichment"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"semantic representation and enrichment of information retrieval experimental data","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-082207","identifier":[{"id":"85019330407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000406746000008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-6e89ec7c-f172-4dd2-94c6-2e084bc70c9f"],"keyword":["Experimental data","Expert search","Expertise profiling","Information retrieval evaluation","Resource description framework","Semantic enrichment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CD116EA6BC84E421E17925B2A4985EA"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"university of galway","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Galway","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianmaria","key":"silvellopau","last":"Silvello","name":"Silvello, Gianmaria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgeta","key":"bordeapau","last":"Bordea","name":"Bordea, Georgeta","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"ferropau","last":"Ferro","name":"Ferro, Nicola","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"buitelaarpau","last":"Buitelaar","name":"Buitelaar, Paul","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00799-016-0172-8","issn":["14321300","14325012"],"issn_org":["14325012"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal on Digital Libraries","pages":"145-172","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"International Journal on Digital Libraries","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019330407"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6e89ec7c-f172-4dd2-94c6-2e084bc70c9f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Semantic representation and enrichment of information retrieval experimental data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-082207","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"There is broad consensus in the field of IR that search is complex in many use cases and applications, both on the Web and in domain-specific collections, and both in our professional and in our daily life. Yet our understanding of complex search tasks, in comparison to simple look up tasks, is fragmented at best. The workshop addressed many open research questions: What are the obvious use cases and applications of complex search? What are essential features of work tasks and search tasks to take into account? And how do these evolve over time? With a multitude of information, varying from introductory to specialized, and from authoritative to speculative or opinionated, when should which sources of information be shown? How does the information seeking process evolve and what are relevant differences between different stages? With complex task and search process management, blending searching, browsing, and recommendations, and supporting exploratory search to sensemaking and analytics, UI and UX design pose an overconstrained challenge. How do we know that our approach is any good? Supporting complex search tasks requires new collaborations across the whole field of IR, and the proposed workshop brought together a diverse group of researchers to work together on one of the greatest challenges of our field. The workshop featured three main elements. First, two keynotes, one on the complexity of meaningful interactive IR evaluation by Mark Hall and one on the types of search complexity encountered in real-world applications by Jussi Karlgren. Second, a lively boaster and poster session in which seven contributed papers were presented. Third, three breakout groups discussed concrete ideas on: (1) search context and tasks, (2) search process, and (3) evaluation of complex search tasks. There was an general feeling that the discussion made progress, and built new connections between related strands of research in IR.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Koolen, Marijn","Kamps, Jaap","Bogers, Toine","Belkin, Nicholas J.","Kelly, Diane","Yilmaz, Emine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071334"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2017-03-11","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2017-03-07","title":"2nd ACM SIGIR Conference on Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","Rutgers - The State University of New Jersey, New Brunswick","University College London","University of Amsterdam","University of Tennessee, Knoxville"],"keyword":["Complex search"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"report on the second workshop on supporting complex search tasks","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sigir.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/p058.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-071334","ids":["aau-4963a2a0-07df-46c7-b7cc-77b83b3c1631"],"keyword":["complex search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C6DA9E8D68293A5B5B7D035217A9E332"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://sigir.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/p058.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"rutgers the state university of new jersey new brunswick","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rutgers - The State University of New Jersey, New Brunswick","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of tennessee knoxville","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Tennessee, Knoxville","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaap","key":"kampspau","last":"Kamps","name":"Kamps, Jaap","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicholas J.","key":"belkinpau","last":"Belkin","name":"Belkin, Nicholas J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Diane","key":"kellypau","last":"Kelly","name":"Kelly, Diane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Emine","key":"yilmazpau","last":"Yilmaz","name":"Yilmaz, Emine","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01635840"],"pages":"58-66","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","series":"SIGIR Forum","status":"p","title":"Report on the Second Workshop on Supporting Complex Search Tasks"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4963a2a0-07df-46c7-b7cc-77b83b3c1631"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Report on the Second Workshop on Supporting Complex Search Tasks","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-071334","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Recommendation algorithms for ratings prediction and item ranking have steadily matured during the past decade. However, these state-of-the-art algorithms are typically applied in relatively straightforward scenarios. In reality, recommendation is often a more complex problem: it is usually just a single step in the user's more complex background need. These background needs can often place a variety of constraints on which recommendations are interesting to the user and when they are appropriate. However, relatively little research has been done on these complex recommendation scenarios. The ComplexRec 2017 workshop addressed this by providing an interactive venue for discussing approaches to recommendation in complex scenarios that have no simple one-size-fits-all-solution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Koolen, Marijn","Mobasher, Bamshad","Said, Alan","Tuzhilin, Alexander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076611"],"event":{"end":"2017-08-31","place":"Como, it","start":"2017-08-27","title":"RecSys 2017: 11th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","DePaul University","New York University","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","University of Skövde"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation","Recommender systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"complexrec 000000002017 recommendation in complex scenarios","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1892/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-076611","ids":["aau-5b806748-a35a-455b-998a-7c1792ace330"],"keyword":["complex recommendation","recommender systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DFD343C9DAF64DC2A4BAFDEE98FB2825"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1892/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"depaul university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DePaul University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"university of skövde","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Skövde","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"new york university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New York University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogersped","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenped","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bamshad","key":"mobasherped","last":"Mobasher","name":"Mobasher, Bamshad","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Alan","key":"saidped","last":"Said","name":"Said, Alan","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"tuzhilinped","last":"Tuzhilin","name":"Tuzhilin, Alexander","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"pages":"28","publisher":"CEUR-WS","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5b806748-a35a-455b-998a-7c1792ace330"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"ComplexRec 2017 : Recommendation in Complex Scenarios","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076611","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"There is broad consensus in the field of IR that search is complex in many use cases and applications, both on the Web and in domain specific collections, and both professionally and in our daily life. Yet our understanding of complex search tasks, in comparison to simple look up tasks, is fragmented at best. The workshop addresses many open research questions: What are the obvious use cases and applications of complex search? What are essential features of work tasks and search tasks to take into account? And how do these evolve over time? With a multitude of information, varying from introductory to specialized, and from authoritative to speculative or opinionated, when to show what sources of information? How does the information seeking process evolve and what are relevant differences between different stages? With complex task and search process management, blending searching, browsing, and recommendations, and supporting exploratory search to sensemaking and analytics, UI and UX design pose an overconstrained challenge. How do we evaluate and compare approaches? Which measures should be taken into account? Supporting complex search tasks requires new collaborations across the fields of CHI and IR, and the proposed workshop will bring together a diverse group of researchers to work together on one of the greatest challenges of our field.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Belkin, Nick","Bogers, Toine","Kamps, Jaap","Kelly, Diane","Koolen, Marijn","Yilmaz, Emine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-096396"],"event":{"end":"2017-03-11","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2017-03-07","title":"2nd ACM SIGIR Conference on Information Interaction and Retrieval, CHIIR 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Koolen, Marijn"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","Rutgers - The State University of New Jersey, New Brunswick","University College London","University of Amsterdam","University of Tennessee, Knoxville"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"second workshop on supporting complex search tasks","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85016951239&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-096396","identifier":[{"id":"85016951239","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9fea4ba5-9377-46ba-a236-6285fac8da69"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DD99F591FB6444374EDD14BC9F57192"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"rutgers the state university of new jersey new brunswick","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rutgers - The State University of New Jersey, New Brunswick","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Eu