{"abstract":"Book search is far from a solved problem. Complex information needs often go beyond bibliographic facts and cover a combination of different aspects, such as specific genres or plot elements, engagement or novelty. Conventional book metadata may not be sufficient to address these kinds of information needs. In this paper, we present a large-scale empirical comparison of the effectiveness of book metadata elements for searching complex information needs. Using a test collection of over 2 million book records and over 330 real-world book search requests, we perform a highly controlled and in-depth analysis of topical metadata, comparing controlled vocabularies with social tags. Tags perform better overall in this setting, but controlled vocabulary terms provide complementary information, which will improve a search. We analyze potential underlying factors that contribute to search performance, such as the relevance aspect(s) mentioned in a request or the type of book. In addition, we investigate the possible causes of search failure. We conclude that neither tags nor controlled vocabularies are wholly suited to handling the complex information needs in book search, which means that different approaches to describe topical information in books are needed.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Petras, Vivien"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080097"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Book search","Controlled vocabularies","Failure analysis","Query analysis","Social tagging"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"supporting book search a comprehensive comparison of tags vs controlled vocabulary metadata","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/dim-2017-0004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-080097","identifier":[{"id":"85057275610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-67735b4b-0eaa-43a2-8a1b-d06b8a00e71e"],"keyword":["book search","controlled vocabularies","failure analysis","query analysis","social tagging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ADC8B376102DEA7BD0B572395E7D6B57"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 3.0","type":"rem","url":"https://www.degruyter.com/view/j/dim.2017.1.issue-1/dim-2017-0004/dim-2017-0004.xml?format=INT","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/dim-2017-0004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/287473513/_25439251_Data_and_Information_Management_Supporting_Book_Search_A_Comprehensive_Comparison_of_Tags_vs._Controlled_Vocabulary_Metadata_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/dim-2017-0004","issn":["25439251"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Data and Information Management","pages":"17-34","publisher":"De Gruyter Mouton","status":"p","title":"Journal of Data and Information Management","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057275610"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-67735b4b-0eaa-43a2-8a1b-d06b8a00e71e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Supporting Book Search : A Comprehensive Comparison of Tags vs. Controlled Vocabulary Metadata","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-080097","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Book search for information needs that go beyond standard bibliographic data is far from a solved problem. Such complex information needs often cover a combination of di erent aspects, such as specific genres or plot elements, engagement or novelty. By design, subject information in controlled vocabularies is not always adequate in covering such complex needs, and social tags have been proposed as an alternative. In this paper we present a large-scale empirical comparison and in-depth analysis of the value of controlled vocabularies and tags for book retrieval using a test collection of over 2 million book records and over 330 real-world book information needs. We find that while tags and controlled vocabulary terms provide complementary performance, tags perform better overall. However, this is not due to a popularity e ect; instead, tags are better at matching the language of regular users. Finally, we perform a detailed failure analysis and show, using tags and controlled vocabulary terms, that some request types are inherently more di cult to solve than others.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Petras, Vivien"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090429"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2017-03-25","place":"Wuhan, cn","start":"2017-03-22","title":"iConference 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Book search","Controlled vocabularies","Failure analysis","Query analysis","Social tagging"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an in depth analysis of tags and controlled metadata for book search","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.9776/17002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090429","ids":["aau-8add7d1f-5348-4dd6-8d05-26469cd8e736"],"keyword":["book search","controlled vocabularies","failure analysis","query analysis","social tagging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-A09FA26C030CB911BCF01D5E79F75F71"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.9776/17002","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/296092551/iconf2017_tagging_analysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/bitstream/handle/2142/98869/2pt2_Bogers-Tags.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.9776/17002","isbn":["9780988490048"],"issn":["23256850"],"publisher":"iSchools","series":"iConference Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of iConference 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8add7d1f-5348-4dd6-8d05-26469cd8e736"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"An In-Depth Analysis of Tags and Controlled Metadata for Book Search","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-090429","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Research into recommendation algorithms has made great strides in recent years. However, these algorithms are typically applied in relatively straightforward scenarios: given information about a user's past preferences, what will they like in the future? Recommendation is often more complex: evaluating recommended items never takes place in a vacuum, and it is often a single step in the user's more complex background task. In this paper, we define a specific type of recommendation scenario called narrative-driven recommendation, where the recommendation process is driven by both a log of the user's past transactions as well as a narrative description of their current interest(s). Through an analysis of a set of real-world recommendation narratives from the LibraryThing forums, we demonstrate the uniqueness and richness of this scenario and highlight common patterns and properties of such narratives.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Koolen, Marijn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-117107"],"event":{"acronym":"RecSys","end":"2017-08-31","place":"Como, it","start":"2017-08-27","title":"RecSys 2017: 11th ACM Conference on Recommender Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences"],"keyword":["Complex recommendation","Narrative driven Recommendation","Query driven recommendation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"defining and supporting narrative driven recommendation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-117107","identifier":[{"id":"85030449555","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000426967000036","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-e6c6fa16-7cec-438d-9441-1f0c78f5ff35"],"keyword":["complex recommendation","conversational recommenders","narrative-driven recommendation","query-driven recommendation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-817183E032E82D12B6488B57E89FBD83"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3109859.3109893","eisbn":["9781450346528"],"pages":"238-242","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"RecSys '17","title":"Proceedings of the Eleventh ACM Conference on Recommender Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85030449555"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e6c6fa16-7cec-438d-9441-1f0c78f5ff35"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Defining and Supporting Narrative-driven Recommendation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-117107","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
