Aalborg University"],"title":"Preface","type":"Editorial","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068507","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present an overview of the mining track in the Social Book Search (SBS) lab 2016. The mining track addressed two tasks: (1) classifying forum posts as book search requests, and (2) linking book title mentions in forum posts to unique book IDs in a database. Both tasks are important steps in the process of solving complex search tasks within online reader communities. We prepared two data collections for the classification task: posts from the LibraryThing (LT) forum and a smaller number of posts from Reddit. For the linking task we used annotated LT threads. We found that the classification task was relatively straightforward, achieving up to 94% classification accuracy. The book linking task on the other hand turned out to be a difficult task: here the best system achieved an accuracy of 41% and F-score of 33.5%. Both the automatic classification of book search requests as the automatic linking of book mentions could next year be part of the pipeline for processing complex book searches.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Hendrickx, Iris","Koolen, Marijn","Verberne, Suzan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-090391"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2016-09-08","place":"Évora, pt","start":"2016-09-05","title":"Conference and Labs of the Evaluation forum","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huygens Institute of Netherlands History","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"keyword":["Book search","Information retrieval","Text mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overview of the sbs 000000002016 mining track","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/281622522/16091053.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-090391","identifier":[{"id":"85019586925","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8ab914a4-ac3a-409a-9f28-6a8927b185b9"],"keyword":["book search","forum mining","information retrieval","text mining"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-EEA52E58327A3E518135A3D3C8286811"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/281622522/16091053.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-1609/16091053.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"huygens institute of netherlands history","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Huygens Institute of Netherlands History","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Iris","key":"hendrickxpau","last":"Hendrickx","name":"Hendrickx, Iris","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Suzan","key":"verbernepau","last":"Verberne","name":"Verberne, Suzan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Krisztian","key":"balogpedh","last":"Balog","name":"Balog, Krisztian","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"capellatopedh","last":"Capellato","name":"Capellato, Linda","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Nicola","key":"ferropedh","last":"Ferro","name":"Ferro, Nicola","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Craig","key":"mcdonaldpedh","last":"McDonald","name":"McDonald, Craig","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"pages":"1053-1063","publisher":"CEUR-WS","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Working Notes of CLEF 2016 - Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019586925"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8ab914a4-ac3a-409a-9f28-6a8927b185b9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Overview of the SBS 2016 Mining Track","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-090391","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"English content still dominates in many online domains and information systems, despite native English speakers being a minority of its users. However, we know little about how language proficiency influences search behavior in these systems. In this paper, we describe preliminary results from an interactive IR experiment with book search behavior and examine how language skills affect this behavior. A total of 97 users from 21 different countries participated in this experiment, resulting in a rich data set including usage data as well as questionnaire feedback. Although participants reported feeling language constraints, a preliminary analysis of native and non-native English speakers indicate little to no meaningful differences in their search behavior.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Gäde, Maria","Hall, Mark M.","Skov, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-122975"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2016-03-23","place":"Philadelphia, PA, us","start":"2016-03-20","title":"iConference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Edge Hill University","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyzing the influence of language proficiency on interactive book search behavior","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.9776/16010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-122975","ids":["aau-fb0e83d1-a9af-460b-a4b4-7138afbe94da"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7C1A552F871C725509C5DAD673B95A65"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.9776/16010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/bitstream/handle/2142/89335/Bogers554.pdf?sequence=1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"edge hill university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Edge Hill University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"gädepau","last":"Gäde","name":"Gäde, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark M.","key":"hallpau","last":"Hall","name":"Hall, Mark M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.9776/16010","isbn":["9780988490024"],"publisher":"iSchools","status":"p","subtitle":"Partnership with Society","title":"Proceedings of iConference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fb0e83d1-a9af-460b-a4b4-7138afbe94da"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analyzing the Influence of Language Proficiency on Interactive Book Search Behavior","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-122975","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"One of the determining factors of the quality of Web search engines is the size of their index. In addition to its influence on search result quality, the size of the indexed Web can also tell us something about which parts of the WWW are directly accessible to the everyday user. We propose a novel method of estimating the size of a Web search engine’s index by extrapolating from document frequencies of words observed in a large static corpus of Web pages. In addition, we provide a unique longitudinal perspective on the size of Google and Bing’s indices over a nine-year period, from March 2006 until January 2015. We find that index size estimates of these two search engines tend to vary dramatically over time, with Google generally possessing a larger index than Bing. This result raises doubts about the reliability of previous one-off estimates of the size of the indexed Web. We find that much, if not all of this variability can be explained by changes in the indexing and ranking infrastructure of Google and Bing. This casts further doubt on whether Web search engines can be used reliably for cross-sectional webometric studies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Van den Bosch, Antal","Bogers, Toine","De Kunder, Maurice"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-110231"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","De Kunder Internet Media","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"keyword":["Index size estimation","Longitudinal study","Search engines","Webometrics"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimating search engine index size variability a 000000000009 year longitudinal study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11192-016-1863-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-110231","identifier":[{"id":"000376273600029","type":"wos"},{"id":"84957638868","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-cf45c9eb-b0f5-4e26-8530-6a41e6f5cc4a"],"keyword":["Index size estimation","Longitudinal study","Search engines","Webometrics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0683C07C4FFF8E1821ED6550E06A3E01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/227976830/Van_den_Bosch_et_al._2016_Estimating_Search_Engine_Index_Size_Variability_A_9_Year_Longitudinal_Study_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s11192-016-1863-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"de kunder internet media","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"De Kunder Internet Media","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Antal","key":"vandenboschpau","last":"Van den Bosch","name":"Van den Bosch, Antal","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurice","key":"dekunderpau","last":"De Kunder","name":"De Kunder, Maurice","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11192-016-1863-z","issn":["01389130","15882861"],"issn_org":["01389130"],"issue":"May","journal":"Scientometrics","pages":"839-856","publisher":"Akadémiai Kiadó","status":"p","title":"Scientometrics","volume":"107"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957638868"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cf45c9eb-b0f5-4e26-8530-6a41e6f5cc4a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimating Search Engine Index Size Variability : A 9-Year Longitudinal Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-110231","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Experimental evaluation carried out in international large-scale campaigns is a fundamental pillar of the scientific and technological advancement of Information Retrieval (IR) systems. Such evaluation activities produce a large quantity of scientific and experimental data, which are the foundation for all the subsequent scientific production and development of new systems. We discuss how to annotate and interlink this data, by proposing a method for exposing experimental data as Linked Open Data (LOD) on the Web and as a basis for enriching and automatically connecting this data with expertise topics and expert profiles. In this context, a topiccentric approach for expert search is proposed, addressing the extraction of expertise topics, their semantic grounding with the LOD cloud, and their connection to IR experimental data.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Bordea, Georgeta","Buitelaar, Paul","Ferro, Nicola","Silvello, Gianmaria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-093265"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-07","place":"Napoli, it","start":"2016-12-05","title":"3rd Italian Conference on Computational Linguistics, CLiC-it 2016 and 5th Evaluation Campaign of Natural Language Processing and Speech Tools for Italian, EVALITA 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Ireland","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Galway","University of Padua"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ir scientific data how to semantically represent and enrich them","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85009259773&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-093265","identifier":[{"id":"85009259773","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-94f687c2-9ef8-4443-ac85-60d691c93ad9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-67E22E057638E292A701DAEF70D59E14"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"university of galway","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Galway","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"university of padua","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Padua","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgeta","key":"bordeapau","last":"Bordea","name":"Bordea, Georgeta","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"buitelaarpau","last":"Buitelaar","name":"Buitelaar, Paul","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"ferropau","last":"Ferro","name":"Ferro, Nicola","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gianmaria","key":"silvellopau","last":"Silvello","name":"Silvello, Gianmaria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"1749"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85009259773"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94f687c2-9ef8-4443-ac85-60d691c93ad9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"IR Scientific data : How to semantically represent and enrich them","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-093265","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A fair review process is essential to the success of any scientific conference. In this paper we present an analysis of the reviewing process of the 2014-2015 iConferences as well as a demographic analysis of the iConference community as a whole. The results show a clear need for making the reviewer pool more representative of the iSchool community as a whole by including more women and more researchers from Asian institutions. Other recommendations are to improve the continuity of the reviewer pool and to provide clearer instructions to reviewers to ensure that written reviews explicitly cover all the aspects represented by the review scores. The results of our study provide the iSchool community with a descriptive analysis of its community and a better understanding of its review process.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Greifeneder, Elke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121622"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2016-03-23","place":"Philadelphia, PA, us","start":"2016-03-20","title":"iConference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the ischool community a case study of iconference reviews","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/bitstream/handle/2142/89312/Bogers247.pdf?sequence=1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121622","ids":["aau-f645ab32-4ed7-4b2c-af40-2f3670953915"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-25374CD5F6014CFFBC4774B5AE5CF7B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/bitstream/handle/2142/89312/Bogers247.pdf?sequence=1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elke","key":"greifenederpau","last":"Greifeneder","name":"Greifeneder, Elke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9780988490024"],"publisher":"iSchools","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of iConference 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f645ab32-4ed7-4b2c-af40-2f3670953915"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The iSchool Community : A Case Study of iConference Reviews","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121622","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"While content-based recommendation has been applied successfully in many different domains, it has not seen the same level of attention as collaborative filtering techniques have. However, there are many recommendation domains and applications where content and metadata play a key role, either in addition to or instead of ratings and implicit usage data. For some domains, such as movies, the relationship between content and usage data has seen thorough investigation already, but for many other domains, such as books, news, scientific articles, and Web pages we still do not know if and how these data sources should be combined to provided the best recommendation performance. The CBRecSys 2016 workshop provides a dedicated venue for papers dedicated to all aspects of content-based recommendation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Lops, Pasquale","Koolen, Marijn","Musto, Cataldo","Semeraro, Giovanni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-071619"],"event":{"end":"2016-09-19","place":"Boston, MA, us","start":"2016-09-15","title":"RecSys 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Huygens Institute of Netherlands History","Università Degli Studi Di Bari Aldo Moro"],"keyword":["Context","Recommender systems","Semantics","User generated content","content based recommendation","implicit feedback","text reviews"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cbrecsys 000000002016 new trends on content based recommender systems proceedings of the 000000000003rd workshop on new trends on content based recommender systems co located with 000000000010th acm conference on recommender systems recsys 000000002016",