{"abstract":"In this paper we describe our participation in the Interactive Social Book Search task at CLEF 2015. We focus our analysis on differences in search behaviour between native and non-native speakers of English. The analysis is based on both questionnaire and log data. 49 participants out of the 192 total participants are native speakers and the remaining 143 participants are nonnative speakers. In general results show surprisingly few differences in search behaviour between native and non-native speakers. Non-native speakers spent more time on both the focused and the open task than the native speakers, but no significant differences were found in relation to number of queries, query length, depth of results inspection, number of books added to the book-bag, or length of notes explaining why a book was added to the book-bag.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skov, Mette","Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-078457"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2015-09-11","place":"Toulouse, fr","start":"2015-09-08","title":"CLEF 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Information seeking","Interactive IR","Social book search"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the influence of language proficiency on book search behaviour","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/229504016/Skov_Bogers_2015_The_influence_of_language_proficiency_on_book_search_behaviour.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-078457","identifier":[{"id":"84982833792","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-61e69099-ee34-4a75-95f7-ff0ea9a03fd2"],"keyword":["Information seeking","Interactive IR","interactive book search","social book search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8B9BBA3FEA31ACA4CE469BE85F3645F1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/229504016/Skov_Bogers_2015_The_influence_of_language_proficiency_on_book_search_behaviour.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, E-learning lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"1fefa70a-ff67-4c75-8b7a-021837757980","name":"Skov, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-8821-0314","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"cappellatopedh","last":"Cappellato","name":"Cappellato, Linda","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ferro","key":"nicolapedh","last":"Nicola","name":"Nicola, Ferro","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gareth J. F.","key":"jonespedh","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Gareth J. F.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eric San","key":"juanpedh","last":"Juan","name":"Juan, Eric San","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"publisher":"CEUR-WS","series":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Working Notes of CLEF2015 - Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982833792"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-61e69099-ee34-4a75-95f7-ff0ea9a03fd2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The Influence of Language Proficiency on Book Search Behaviour","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-078457","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Real-world information needs are generally complex, yet almost all research focuses instead on either relatively simple search based on queries or recommendation based on profiles. It is difficult to gain insight into complex information needs from observational studies with existing systems; potentially complex needs are obscured by the systems’ limitations. In this paper we study explicit information requests in social media, focusing on the rich area of social book search. We analyse a large set of annotated book requests from the LibraryThing discussion forums. We investigate 1) the comprehensiveness of book requests on the forums, 2) what relevance aspects are expressed in real-world book search requests, and 3) how different types of search topics are related to types of users, human recommendations, and results returned by retrieval and recommender systems. We find that book search requests combine search and recommendation aspects in intricate ways that require more than only traditional search or (hybrid) recommendation approaches.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Koolen, Marijn","Bogers, Toine","Jaap, Kamps","Van den Bosch, Antal"],"cuid":["S02-080.00-715728"],"event":{"acronym":"ECIR(CONF)","end":"2015-04-02","place":"Vienna, at","start":"2015-03-29","title":"37th European Conference on Information Retrieval","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Nijmegen","University of Amsterdam"],"keyword":["Book search","Evaluation","Information retrieval","Recommendation","Social media"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"looking for books in social media an analysis of complex search requests","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/211499913/ecir15.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-080.00-715728","identifier":[{"id":"84925398259","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-951f5141-7e6c-4e38-ad71-c5bf90f583fb","itu-88e8c496-2ccd-404f-8d6e-5cc013e73614"],"keyword":["book search","evaluation","information retrieval","recommendation","social media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E5714FCB354B0F3C1C55EE00024BA293"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/211499913/ecir15.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kamps","key":"jaappau","last":"Jaap","name":"Jaap, Kamps","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaap","key":"kampspau","last":"Kamps","name":"Kamps, Jaap","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Antal","key":"vandenboschpau","last":"Van den Bosch","name":"Van den Bosch, Antal","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Allan","key":"hanburypedh","last":"Hanbury","name":"Hanbury, Allan","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gabriella","key":"kazaipedh","last":"Kazai","name":"Kazai, Gabriella","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"rauberpedh","last":"Rauber","name":"Rauber, Andreas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Norbert","key":"fuhrpedh","last":"Fuhr","name":"Fuhr, Norbert","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-16354-3_19","eisbn":["9783319163543"],"isbn":["9783319163536"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"184-196","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"37th European Conference on IR Research, ECIR 2015, Vienna, Austria, March 29 - April 2, 2015. Proceedings","title":"Advances in Information Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925398259"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-951f5141-7e6c-4e38-ad71-c5bf90f583fb","itu-88e8c496-2ccd-404f-8d6e-5cc013e73614"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Looking for Books in Social Media : An Analysis of Complex Search Requests","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.00-715728","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The goal of the SBS 2015 Suggestion Track is to evaluate approaches for supporting users in searching collections of books who express their information needs both in a query and through example books. The track investigates the complex nature of relevance in book search and the role of traditional and user-generated book metadata in retrieval. We extended last year's investigation into the nature of book suggestions from the LibraryThing forums and how they compare to book relevance judgements. Participants were encouraged to incorporate rich user profiles of both topic creators and other LibraryThing users to explore the relative value of recommendation and retrieval paradigms for book search. We found further support that such suggestions are a valuable alternative to traditional test collections that are based on top-k pooling and editorial relevance judgements. In terms of systems evaluation, the most effective systems include some form of learning-to-rank. It seems that the complex nature of the requests and the book descriptions, with multiple sources of evidence, requires a careful balancing of system parameters.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Koolen, Marijn","Bogers, Toine","Kamps, Jaap"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058857"],"event":{"acronym":"CLEF","end":"2015-09-11","place":"Toulouse, fr","start":"2015-09-08","title":"16th Conference and Labs of the Evaluation Forum, CLEF 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Amsterdam"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overview of the sbs 000000002015 suggestion track","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84982786678&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-058857","identifier":[{"id":"84982786678","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1e295a0b-0678-483a-8c3b-2679194f6c4c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3E51F1B327E203BDAA471DCAAA4125BB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of amsterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Amsterdam","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marijn","key":"koolenpau","last":"Koolen","name":"Koolen, Marijn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaap","key":"kampspau","last":"Kamps","name":"Kamps, Jaap","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16130073"],"journal":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","publisher":"CEUR-WS","status":"p","title":"CEUR Workshop Proceedings","volume":"1391"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84982786678"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1e295a0b-0678-483a-8c3b-2679194f6c4c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Overview of the SBS 2015 suggestion track","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058857","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The popularity of social tagging has sparked a great deal of debate on whether tags could replace or improve upon professional metadata as descriptors of books and other information objects. In this paper we present a large-scale empirical comparison of the contributions of individual information elements like core bibliographic data, controlled vocabulary terms, reviews, and tags to the retrieval performance. Our comparison is done using a test collection of over 2 million book records with information elements from Amazon, the British Library, the Library of Congress, and LibraryThing. We find that tags and controlled vocabulary terms do not actually outperform each other consistently, but seem to provide complementary contributions: some information needs are best addressed using controlled vocabulary terms whereas other are best addressed using tags.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Petras, Vivien"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-110236"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2015-03-27","place":"Newport Beach, CA, us","start":"2015-03-24","title":"iConference 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Humboldt University of Berlin"],"keyword":["Book search","Controlled vocabularies","Indexing","Social tagging"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tagging vs controlled vocabulary which is more helpful for book search","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/229500993/PDF.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-110236","ids":["aau-cf47b56e-9020-421e-b0d8-bc6503418923"],"keyword":["book search","controlled vocabularies","indexing","social tagging"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FD2CF0F359A6155A000AC027C5873FA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/229500993/PDF.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/handle/2142/73673","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"humboldt university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt University of Berlin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivien","key":"petraspau","last":"Petras","name":"Petras, Vivien","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"iSchools","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of iConference 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cf47b56e-9020-421e-b0d8-bc6503418923"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Tagging vs. Controlled Vocabulary : Which is More Helpful for Book Search?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-110236","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Despite a surge in popularity of work on casual leisure search, some leisure domains are still relatively underrepresented. Movies are good example of such a domain, which is peculiar given the popularity of movie-centered websites and discovery services such as IMDB, RottenTomatoes, and Netflix. In this paper, we present an exploratory analysis of IMDB movie discussion threads that contain requests for movies to watch. Through emergent coding we produce a taxonomy of relevance aspects for movie search and selection. Our analysis shows that topical aspects, such as content, metadata, and known-item search, are important for movie selection practices. Other requests focus more on recommendation and feature many subjective relevance aspects, such as the tone of a movie or its intended audience. This suggests efficient access to movies is likely to require different information access paradigms to satisfy all the movie-related information needs expressed in the threads.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121620"],"event":{"acronym":"iConference","end":"2015-03-27","place":"Newport Beach, CA, us","start":"2015-03-24","title":"iConference 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Everyday life","Information behavior","Information seeking","Movies","Recommendation","Relevance","SEARCH"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"searching for movies an exploratory analysis of movie related information needs","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/211306583/iconf2015_analyzing_movie_needs.CAMERA_READY.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121620","ids":["aau-f64482e3-812d-4cd8-a225-ba7412cf4763"],"keyword":["everyday life","information behavior","information seeking","movies","recommendation","relevance","search"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-02647EE7880476E0ADFCEFD0DC2E52DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/211306583/iconf2015_analyzing_movie_needs.CAMERA_READY.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.illinois.edu/handle/2142/73689","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Communication and Information Studies (CIS)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"c39fa087-a00a-425e-9e0f-7fa301dbe554","name":"Bogers, Toine","orcid":"0000-0003-0716-676X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"iSchools","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of iConference 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f64482e3-812d-4cd8-a225-ba7412cf4763"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Searching for Movies : An Exploratory Analysis of Movie-related Information Needs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121620","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"INEX investigates focused retrieval from structured documents by providing large test collections of structured documents, uniform evaluation measures, and a forum for organizations to compare their results. This paper reports on the INEX 2014 evaluation campaign, which consisted of three tracks: The Interactive Social Book Search Track investigated user information seeking behavior when interacting with various sources of information, for realistic task scenarios, and how the user interface impacts search and the search experience. The Social Book Search Track investigated the relative value of authoritative metadata and user-generated content for search and recommendation using a test collection with data from Amazon and LibraryThing, including user profiles and personal catalogues. The Tweet Contextualization Track investigated tweet contextualization, helping a user to understand a tweet by providing him with a short background summary generated from relevant Wikipedia passages aggregated into a coherent summary. INEX 2014 was an exciting year for INEX in which we for the third time ran our workshop as part of the CLEF labs. This paper gives an overview of all the INEX 2014 tracks, their aims and task, the built test-collections, the participants, and gives an initial analysis of the results.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Bellot, Patrice","Bogers, Toine","Geva, Shlomo","Hall, Mark","Huurdeman, Hugo","Kamps, Jaap","Kazai, Gabriella","Koolen, Marijn","Moriceau, Veronique","Mothe, Josiane","Preminger, Michael","SanJuan, Eric","Schenkel, Ralf","Skov, Mette","Tannier, Xavier","Walsh, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718846"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queensland University of Technology","University of Amsterdam","University of Passau"],"keywor