 Marinus","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"1c118aa8-cea9-41c8-94dd-cba3065ee1be","name":"Bogers, Toine","name_org":"Bogers, Antonius Marinus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Haakon","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"9c53d393-1183-4199-8c76-bce14fc340ad","name":"Lund, Haakon","orcid":"0000-0002-0650-6702","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maj Lauge","key":"wardjensenpau","last":"Ward Jensen","name":"Ward Jensen, Maj Lauge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Erik","key":"wistruppau","last":"Wistrup","name":"Wistrup, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Birger","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3683438d-2cbb-4583-a99d-1b8ed50be5ce","name":"Larsen, Birger","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pamela","key":"fornerpedh","last":"Forner","name":"Forner, Pamela","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Roberto","key":"naviglipedh","last":"Navigli","name":"Navigli, Roberto","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dan","key":"tufispedh","last":"Tufis","name":"Tufis, Dan","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788890481055"],"status":"p","subtitle":"Online Working Notes 23 - 26 September, Valencia, Spain","title":"CLEF 2013 Evaluation Labs and Workshop"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fce1cae2-47d8-4d50-b3c1-e139fdc99613"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RSLIS/AAU at CHiC 2013","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779602","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we present work on micro-serendipity: investigating everyday contexts, conditions, and attributes of serendipity as shared on Twitter. In contrast to related work, we deliberately omit a preset definition of serendipity to allow for the inclusion of micro-occurrences of what people themselves consider as meaningful coincidences in everyday life. We find that different people have different thresholds for what they consider serendipitous, revealing a serendipity continuum. We propose a distinction between background serendipity (or ‘traditional’ serendipity) and foreground serendipity (or ‘synchronicity’, unexpectedly finding something meaningful related to foreground interests). Our study confirms the presence of three key serendipity elements of unexpectedness, insight and value (Makri & Blandford, 2012), and suggests a fourth element, preoccupation (foreground problem/interest), which covers synchronicity. Finally, we find that a combination of features based on word usage, POS categories, and hashtag usage show promise in automatically identifying tweets about serendipitous occurrences.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogers, Toine","Björneborn, Lennart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-408869"],"event":{"end":"2013-02-15","place":"Fort Worth, Texas, us","start":"2013-02-12","title":"iConference 2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Everyday life","Information behaviour","Information sharing","Online social networks","Qualitative data analysis","Serendipity","Social computing","Twitter","quantitative data analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"micro serendipity meaningful coincidences in everyday life shared on twitter","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/47031018/Bogers_2013_Micro_serendipity_Meaningful_Coincidences_in_Everyday_Life_Shared_on_Twitter_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-408869","ids":["ku-19d58926-bdc2-4a6f-83bf-d647a6895ba6"],"keyword":["Twitter","everyday life","information behaviour","information sharing","online social networks","qualitative data analysis","quantitative data analysis","serendipity","social and community informatics","social computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-F70771E064D057BFC1426102DB4DCD60"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/47031018/Bogers_2013_Micro_serendipity_Meaningful_Coincidences_in_Everyday_Life_Shared_on_Twitter_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.9776/13175","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ideals.uiuc.edu/handle/2142/36052","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication, Department of Information Studies (INF)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Toine","key":"bogerspau","last":"Bogers","locid":"1c118aa8-cea9-41c8-94dd-cba3065ee1be","name":"Bogers, Toine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lennart","key":"björnebornpau","last":"Björneborn","locid":"35ed087e-1484-41c5-accd-e947d622b2b1","name":"Björneborn, Lennart","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.9776/13175","pages":"196-208","place":"IDEALS","publisher":"iSchools","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the iConference 2013"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-19d58926-bdc2-4a6f-83bf-d647a6895ba6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Micro-serendipity: Meaningful Coincidences in Everyday Life Shared on Twitter","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408869","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
